    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G69190-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G69190-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q1ENB6" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding a cytosolic form of the bifunctional hydroxymethyldihydropterin pyrophosphokinase/ dihydropteroate synthase (HPPK/DHPS) has been identified and characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme catalyzes two consecutive steps in the tetrahydrofolate biosynthetic pathway, i.e. the diphosphorylation of dihyropterin (HPPK activity) and the following incorporation of p-aminobenzoate (pABA) to finally form dihydropteroate (DHPS avtivity). The molecular function was confirmed by two lines of evidence, first the functional complementation of a yeast mutant and second by characterizing the recombinant protein expressed in and obtained from &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. This enzyme is located at a branchpoint of the tetrahydrofolate biosynthesis, therefore considered to have regulating impact on the pathway. The exclusive expression of the enzyme in the developing inflorescence indicates a function in sustaining the high rate of DNA synthesis during this process to boost folate supplies. In addition, a function related to oxidative stress has been proposed due to the decreased germination rate in the corresponding knock-out mutant seed during development. However, the &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; function of the enzyme remains elusive as its mitochondrial counterpart (mitHPPK/DHPS - At4g3000) is considered to be sufficient to contribute to the folate biosynthesis. Therefore, the cytHPPK/DHPS is considered a unique feature in Arabidopsis probably created by a relatively recent gene duplication |CITS: [17289662]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G69190-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G69190.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q1ENB6" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="CAI29255" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-9639, RXN-4541" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005829" />
