    <DataNode elementId="AT1G68760-MONOMER" textLabel="8-oxo-dGTP pyrophosphohydrolase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9CA40" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">NUDX1 is a member of the nudix (NUcleotide DIphosphates linked to some moiety X) family of hydrolases. Although it was originally thought to act as an |FRAME: RXN0-1441 &quot;NADH pyrophosphatase&quot;| based on assays performed in the presence of 5 mM |FRAME: MN+2 Mn&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|, subsequent analyses executed in the presence of |FRAME: MG+2 Mg&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;| indicate that &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; this enzyme is may be bi-functional and active against 8-oxo-(d)GTP and dihydroneopterin triphosphate |CITS: [15878881][17804481][15611104]|. 8-oxo-(d)GTP can be formed spontaneously in the cell by reactive oxygen species. It can then be mis-incorporated into DNA or RNA and cause errors in DNA replication and transcription. Organisms, from bacteria to humans, therefore have enzymes like NUDX1 that can cleave the diphosphate group from these oxidized nucleotides and prevent them from being added to nascent DNA and RNA strands |CITS: [17804481]|. NUDX1 also has similarity to a bacterial enzyme involved in folate synthase that acts on DHNTP. NUDX1 can catalyze the formation of DHNP from this compound, but kinetic analyses of the enzyme demonstrate that it prefers 8-oxo-(d)GTP and other nucleoside triphosphates to NUDX1 may form a dimer under native conditions |CITS: [12399474]|. It has a k&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt; / K&lt;sub&gt;m&lt;/sub&gt; of 1.0 x 10&lt;sup&gt;4&lt;/sup&gt; s&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; M&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; |CITS: [12399474]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G68760-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G68760.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9CA40" />
