    <DataNode elementId="AT5G57850-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G57850-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8L493" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="555" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The protein sequence of aminodeoxychorismate lyase (ADCL) of E. coli (PabC) was used to locate cognate ESTs and isolate the cDNA encoding the ADCL in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The functional complementation of an &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; mutant lacking ADC lyase activity confirmed that the cDNA indeed encoded for a functional enzyme |CITS: [15500462]|. The complemented enzyme was recombinant expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; bearing the ADC synthase gene |CITS: [14745019]| demonstrating in this coupled assay the formation of p-aminobenzoate (pABA). The dimeric protein was not inhibited by physiological concentrations of folates, pABA, or pABAglucose ester. The plastidal subcellular localization was confirmed by import assays in isolated pea chloroplasts fusing the Arabidopsis ADCL cDNA to the green fluorescent protein (GFP) |CITS: [15500462]|. The function of this protein and the interaction of its two domains has been further characterized &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; using recombinant proteins expressed in E.coli |CITS: [20851095]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G57850-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G57850.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11825" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q8L493" />
